devtools: devtools.styleLint (TARGET)
devtools: devtools.styleLint (TARGET, RULES)
devtools: R = devtools.styleLint (...)
Check code against the layout rules of the Octave packages' coding style.

devtools.styleLint (TARGET) prints every line that breaks one
of the rules below. TARGET is one file, the folder a package's
source is in, or the name of an installed package.

devtools.styleLint (TARGET, RULES) checks only the rules
named in RULES, a cell array of character vectors. The rules are
one maintainer's style rather than anything Octave requires, so each can be
left out.

R = devtools.styleLint (...) prints nothing and returns
the findings as a structure array holding file, line,
column, rule and message, empty where there is nothing
to report. Columns count characters.

The test blocks are code too: a line opening with %! is checked as
the code after its %! prefix, and the body of a %!function
block as the code after %!, its header sitting there.

'tab'
A tab character anywhere, inside a string too, where \t says it
plainly.
'indent'
Two spaces per level of nesting. A case sits two spaces inside its
switch and its body four; else, elseif, catch,
unwind_protect_cleanup and until sit at the level of the line
that opened their block. A comment line takes the level of the next line
of code, or the level of its own block where that line closes or continues
the block, as a comment standing alone in a case does. A section
banner, a comment spanning the page from column one, is exempt. A line
continuing a statement is not checked, whether ... continues it or
an open bracket does.
'quote'
Single quotes are the default for a string. Double quotes are for the
strings passed to error, warning, printf,
fprintf and sprintf, and those are always double, the
strings of a [] or a strcat building one included. The
double quotes are for the message text, so the strings of a warning
state call, warning ('off', id) and the like, are single. A
double-quoted string holding a backslash escape is accepted anywhere,
having no single-quoted spelling.
'length'
A line longer than 80 columns. The lines of a texinfo block are left to
devtools.docLint, and the header of an %!error or
%!warning block is exempt, the message it expects having nowhere
to break.
'condition'
The condition of if, elseif, while and until,
or the value of switch, not in parentheses; or a condition running
over a line with ..., the parentheses continuing it already.

A file that does not parse is reported once as 'syntax', with the
line that stopped it, in place of the rules that read the syntax tree:
'indent', 'quote' and 'condition'. The test blocks
are parsed apart from the code, so either can fail alone.

The parser is a compiled file, so this raises where the package was
installed without a working compiler and a rule reading the syntax tree is
asked for.

See also:
devtools.dialectLint,
devtools.docLint


